uble-digit Harrigan lead consistent with these fundamentals.", "watch": "A major national Democratic wave environment or an unexpected scandal involving Harrigan could pull the race toward competitive territory.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Pat Harrigan (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Pat Harrigan seeks a term representing a western North Carolina district that leans Republican by about nine points. He enters the general election with a large fundraising advantage, more than $1.08 million raised and $451,000 on hand, while Democrat Ashley Bell has raised under $85,000 with minimal outside support. A Libertarian candidate, Steve Feldman, is also on the ballot but has little funding.\n\nAll nine expert ratings place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Democrats only about a 4% chance. A March poll from a Republican-sponsored firm showed Harrigan ahead by roughly fourteen points. With no competitive polling since and no signs of outside investment in the Democratic campaign, the race sits firmly in the Safe Republican category.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0414, "margin": -11.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0292, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0146, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0158, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0277, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0297, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0186, "margin": -13.0}]}